#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092019 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "3e096041-22f8-5b7e-88d7-eca10203a379" :question/math-academy-id "e-5470" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/e8ff769df4089e6ed9a47d56d7317acf41b8aef6a255abc705c0e7ec31a446ea.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/a274b413d20b9aada9f32bc789557097df1a643805c2e8b12c389e3832352c95.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 -  2 \\cdot (-1) = 10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092020 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "e0f036c5-c27d-5a0e-aeb1-cb7c99b49691" :question/math-academy-id "e-5471" :question/problem "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5),$ and $(-2,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/5cb4d5976a3e7153d7041711ab449a1f3af48000021be1d1c4a2c321cbec3467.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/ee8f0cf16983d87fa505303ed6372a3f389518d05b3e13f2e9e2121038792b84.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 -  5 \\cdot (-2) = -11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-11|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "53c7a748-dadb-516e-879b-92cd0c986041" :question/math-academy-id "e-7454" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/4dbe8f14fe2189749e753080658086e4b7f608a5b7028151d2464b99be4a29ed.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|\\det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|2\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|8-3| \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e61c6f39-585c-5789-8871-c80cd6cf4ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "140" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291885} {:answer/id #uuid "6e58b6ca-bc3b-542e-9001-c05b3271b284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "142" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291886} {:answer/id #uuid "3a0a7c6c-51c2-55f6-ab0e-e7f7281d97f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291887} {:answer/id #uuid "633869d6-40e2-5be3-8071-687d67480b55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291888} {:answer/id #uuid "a81129a2-5b02-5192-87ea-4bb9e2c212a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "633869d6-40e2-5be3-8071-687d67480b55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291888} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8cfdd6e-94c6-5377-8e91-d83bb9b39936" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5eeed20e-9ab6-5dbc-851c-1aa1a90bee54" :question/math-academy-id "q-12282" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/fa0dbfe03050a0ca52f2fbe1988a9e6475cd24437c619dba27a4fed984736fc1.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 6=9.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=3\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,8\\,|\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf17624b-ee25-5fa7-8b49-cc1b53d8f418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "279" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343201} {:answer/id #uuid "97ff0b2e-5a45-56b3-84b0-4baebb68ba85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "217" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343202} {:answer/id #uuid "7cfc870e-38df-59be-a12c-3a6faeea4378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343203} {:answer/id #uuid "00f1a4c9-2d3b-5c68-a94b-95d902cb1bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343204} {:answer/id #uuid "9b395d7d-4dda-5ac5-9bdb-e9522f8151af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cfc870e-38df-59be-a12c-3a6faeea4378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343203} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc4cb3b-efc5-5585-a82a-0e0fd4ee886f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7753e17b-6f63-5dc9-9be9-230d0731e05e" :question/math-academy-id "q-164171" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/78c28583961f2588c3e080d227e2e4f20a557ed77dcb20a6332092fe5915b22c.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot (1+2)=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=5\\cdot 7-3\\cdot 9=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,8\\,|\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4ae30c6-ac05-575a-b0f4-76a7ab7caef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4ae30c6-ac05-575a-b0f4-76a7ab7caef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303275} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f393b8e-2297-5b65-897e-ea43622fccaa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "215b2454-d24f-559c-8109-17676c571bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-275983" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,2),(4,6),(6,2).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/a4e507191aecd02e16fafba29598972df423e975dd554b260ca355f0cf6476a1.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 4=8.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-2)=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,6\\,|\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16e1b40d-5e5a-5e30-89c8-edac91f58529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303281} {:answer/id #uuid "3831a940-666b-51f6-878e-71b88512ceae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16e1b40d-5e5a-5e30-89c8-edac91f58529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303281} :answer-field/id #uuid "182ce720-e152-57eb-9369-c8490a44193b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "182ce155-065c-526e-891c-1c2103b06de4" :question/math-academy-id "q-316569" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-10\\cdot 8-9\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|-80-9| \\\\  & =|-89| \\\\  & =89.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab5753c5-998a-5dec-bab6-50b8ad460865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab5753c5-998a-5dec-bab6-50b8ad460865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343208} :answer-field/id #uuid "12894523-9d96-55e8-9907-6c6e3d9e48c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20c83821-7510-5bac-8693-d25d4e5f2268" :question/math-academy-id "q-316571" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 10 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|3\\cdot (-1)-10\\cdot 8| \\\\  & =|-3-80| \\\\  & =|-83| \\\\  & =83.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b7b63de-9ea2-53cb-8d95-b338c5cb7b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b7b63de-9ea2-53cb-8d95-b338c5cb7b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343211} :answer-field/id #uuid "a932832d-e193-5110-b337-2577afa2b9e7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3488dbca-ac22-5a6e-87b9-f563c02c651c" :question/math-academy-id "q-316573" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-6\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot (-4)| \\\\  & =|30-(-4)| \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d1f3828-f31c-570e-948a-c5a959bb229f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343214} {:answer/id #uuid "5e81e5d6-b197-50e5-a23f-d13afa3d0cd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d1f3828-f31c-570e-948a-c5a959bb229f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343214} :answer-field/id #uuid "5abbb853-ab0b-5c4f-97bb-159a62a91d68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fcf34534-2c61-54db-b1c3-099052444c8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-316575" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|9\\cdot 1-(-4)\\cdot 2| \\\\  & =|9-(-8)| \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "376b8af6-29bc-55ae-be7a-9659c2559891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303289} {:answer/id #uuid "38f1d0b5-d56f-5080-be06-dd709d489c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38f1d0b5-d56f-5080-be06-dd709d489c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303290} :answer-field/id #uuid "1965bafe-8660-507f-9547-8ea44caad029" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9258d52-01b3-55d0-afcb-ea66a3cfa2e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-316584" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/f38424364e3d4efd8ebc416974163e3eb87b3350c0c6b8ec7f5ae4ea69339824.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eba14f18-bf0d-54e8-a07d-3286887fc85d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284002} {:answer/id #uuid "b86bf782-71e0-5762-8b4b-387022dd5096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b86bf782-71e0-5762-8b4b-387022dd5096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284003} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc1d744e-1f26-5a9d-b352-65582ed7f9bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "75101661-a27e-5e03-93ec-d54f3d950523" :question/math-academy-id "q-316588" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/cec4f46a70e55735e07cc77fb2013c8d5262ca15feda1ee9eac005a79d38147d.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(4+2)\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-1)\\cdot (-2)-(-2)\\cdot 1=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c04ab0ea-f1d2-59b3-9018-ea51dce54821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c04ab0ea-f1d2-59b3-9018-ea51dce54821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343218} :answer-field/id #uuid "90209ccf-01c5-5b73-8ebd-0624635d0ae4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94ee92da-e759-5ee5-a9ca-480d05dc9adb" :question/math-academy-id "q-316595" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/54537b6712dc9ae74b8b65cd0a14d5d3e878709ae35b2fc5701c7b1a6dd6d044.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(5+2)\\cdot 2=7.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-3)\\cdot 3-0\\cdot 0=-9.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-9\\,|\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =63.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291904 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81001409-c569-533a-a2b7-efcf7f397e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81001409-c569-533a-a2b7-efcf7f397e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291906} :answer-field/id #uuid "f259a8c8-cae9-5672-86ca-ce9c8aca1649" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75fce5ef-ce16-54b6-beee-1ddbfa19c810" :question/math-academy-id "q-316598" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-4)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 1=-12-2=-14.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-14\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46e7464d-7629-5806-aa07-04e5640e39cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284009} {:answer/id #uuid "067bb28f-70ae-5ca2-916c-78f24134099e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "067bb28f-70ae-5ca2-916c-78f24134099e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284010} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c99caa6-f201-5a73-979b-5074f5344bf3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d412caa5-3690-592c-8eec-aa466eedc1b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316606" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1),(5,1),(3,4).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/3e2c56766f201095bee0eea101b877e30910c676c998f37d261fd7cf7aabb837.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-6\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7420781d-c155-5ad9-85a4-980929bb46b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7420781d-c155-5ad9-85a4-980929bb46b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284016} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac4dd13f-f7d6-5ce7-ba52-dcc407db93d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b465aaa4-ff86-5876-9f66-66b7eb23fbbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-316612" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,1),(6,1),(5,4).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/92ee29a22baa10f4af25db8221e7d67c729f5f0f1b5e1b3c37aee7e31a92bdfb.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=4\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-3)=4+3=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,7\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbeb7085-9f03-5a2d-8d0c-2a9fb4e7206c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343221} {:answer/id #uuid "51549d3a-a299-5eb0-a3cc-e0a8aa20680a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343222} {:answer/id #uuid "2a6f90e9-2b52-51db-85f3-8eac9efec00f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343223} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2fa627-8ce3-5105-a06d-17b925f96465" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343224} {:answer/id #uuid "155e6a7a-2f01-5912-9871-9bd38b8813ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51549d3a-a299-5eb0-a3cc-e0a8aa20680a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343222} :answer-field/id #uuid "099a7907-74e2-5da1-82e8-2be2b6a26790" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18981002-6173-5030-9e97-828cf4629e6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-84702" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|(-4)\\cdot 5-3\\cdot (-6)| \\\\  & =|-20+18| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e49c5e39-6bd1-5494-a545-85635d86a202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343228} {:answer/id #uuid "75168d46-dd22-519c-a0b6-7f7d27caa922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343229} {:answer/id #uuid "eba9837d-5e82-5a94-9370-80b6105b5754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343230} {:answer/id #uuid "6be72b2f-e1f7-518b-9c1f-e027bdc503f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343231} {:answer/id #uuid "3de2007d-046b-5b76-a882-bf08014e6c04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75168d46-dd22-519c-a0b6-7f7d27caa922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343229} :answer-field/id #uuid "997872b0-8c67-5e9c-ab87-5c3941600f75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39fcead0-9aa7-5212-bf77-12700c98fa52" :question/math-academy-id "q-9296" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/3cbf4ce4422e043cedb73e9b10bba11e9cb1e64352ff182eff8aaa0046c4e8f3.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,2\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
